<title>USA: Yamana acquires U.S. property.</title>
<headline>Yamana acquires U.S. property.</headline>
<dateline>SPOKANE, Washington 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yamana Resources Inc said on Thursday that it has obtained exploration leases on three prospective properties covering 2,395 acres in northern Washington state.</p>
<p>&quot;All three properties have defined mineral targets -- two gold and one which is primarily copper,&quot; Yamana's executive vice president Dick Walters said in a statement. &quot;We intend to drill them this year.&quot;</p>
<p>The leases are Yamana's entry into North American mineral exploration, the company said. They involve primarily private land and provide standard net smelter royalties to the landowners.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
